# Byte-exact snapshots of the GitHub-HOSTED form of every workflow (scripts/self-hosted-runners/
# hosted-baseline.sh). Reformatting them defeats the entire purpose: the value is the EXACT bytes
# that ran on GitHub-hosted, so a revert is a copy rather than an archaeology exercise. Prettier DID
# rewrite them once (2026-07-16, long `description:` rewrapped) — the live workflows are only
# formatted when staged, so the copies drifted from their own source the moment they were committed.
scripts/self-hosted-runners/hosted-baseline/*.yml

# workspace-manifest.json has a BYTE-CANONICAL contract that prettier CANNOT satisfy, and a QG
# check (scripts/quality_gates/check_workspace_manifest_canonical.py:38) that hard-fails on any
# deviation. Canonical == `json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"`, which ALWAYS
# explodes every array element onto its own line. Prettier (printWidth=120) COLLAPSES any array
# that fits in 120 cols onto one line. The two can never agree, so every local commit that STAGED
# this file was silently reformatted into the non-canonical form by the `prettier-autostage` hook
# (.pre-commit-config.yaml:79-85 — `types_or` includes `json`) and RE-STAGED, i.e. AFTER the author
# had already run quality-gates.sh green. The author's verification could not see it.
#
# Measured 2026-07-17: 73c4449ae ("opt system-integration-tests into ldr_main") intended a ONE-LINE
# promotion_model edit and landed `1 file changed, 95 insertions(+), 431 deletions(-)` — prettier
# collapsing the whole file. That red-lined unified-trading-pm's LDR QG (runs 29576851453 /
# 29576964765 / 29577081402) until the LDR-CI-red monitor INCIDENTALLY healed it: its writer
# (ldr_ci_monitor.py:466-467) is canonical, so persisting one unrelated ldr_ci_status change
# re-exploded the file. That heal only fires when a level actually changes — otherwise PM stays
# RED indefinitely. This is a human-collapses / bot-explodes ping-pong going back to at least
# 2026-06-17 (3f2c6bc89, 06-30, was the exact same edit class).
#
# NOTE: check_workspace_manifest_canonical.py:13 and ci_status_consolidator.py:110-112 both claim
# prettier emits the canonical form. It does not — verified by running prettier on a canonical copy
# and re-checking. That false belief is why this hole stayed open. Fix the docstrings, not this rule.
workspace-manifest.json
